{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/nj1015/posts/jon-bon-jovi-told-20000-people-he-hadnt-heard-a-roar-like-that-in-four-years-and/1064866492607690/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/nj1015/posts/jon-bon-jovi-told-20000-people-he-hadnt-heard-a-roar-like-that-in-four-years-and/1064866492607690/","title":"New Jersey 101.5","description":"Jon Bon Jovi told 20,000 people he hadn't heard a roar like that in four years — and wasn't sure he'd remember what it felt like. That's a moment.","language":"en","text":"Jon Bon Jovi told 20,000 people he hadn't heard a roar like that in four years — and wasn't sure he'd remember what it felt like. That's a moment.\n\nAll reactions:\n\n302 comments\n\n53 shares\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\nNJ1015.COM\n\nBon Jovi's MSG comeback show: full set list and how it actually sounded\n\n### Bon Jovi's MSG comeback show: full set list and how it actually sounded\n\n5\n\nSue SmithKeogh\n\nWait till he hits Croke Park\n\n9\n\nView all 5 replies\n\nJohn Joseph\n\nHe's. Doing excellent....Richie Sambora is not needed 9 sold out shows\n\n23\n\nView all 23 replies\n\nDean Martinez\n\nGood for him and the band!! Nice to see musicians still doing what they love to do, their job which is performing.\n\nWow, so many negative posts. Amazing how some think others actually care what they think by posting negative BS. Makes it seem as if they are just desperate for attention. Why else would you take the time from your life to purposely post a negative comment in what is mostly positive if you’re not desperate for attention.\n\n16\n\nView 1 reply\n\nElena Hernandez\n\nI'm beyond excited ! I will be there July 14th. But, I arrive on July 13th to go shopping for new Bon Jovi Forever attire! Just to be there seeing his beautiful smile again brought me to tears ! I have been a loyal fan for 40 years and counting ! I haven't seen him since 2018. To me, that's an eternity! Wishing Bon Jovi a wonderful tour, and hope to God he adds more dates for others to enjoy around the world !\n\n10\n\nView all 6 replies\n\nDoreen Claridge\n\nWait till tonight baby!!! We are roaring to go!! Koboozs, pen station!!! And the place is jammed with BJ fans!!! Also amazing food and drinks!!! 1.5 hours to go!!!\n\n17\n\nView all 2 replies\n\nChip Vaughn Jr.\n\nI've had the pleasure of meeting him at his restaurant in Tomsriver and have to say he is a hell of a nice guy. I wish him all the best. He and his wife Dorothea are a incredible asset to the community\n\n38\n\nView 1 reply\n\nBonnie Hansen\n\nI was a huge Bon Jovi fan probably saw him nine times I hope for his sake his voices comes back a long way I know he went through a lot to get his singing voice back it's not the same as it was but I always liked him I'm wishing him the very best on his tours\n\n3\n\nDenise Stiebris\n\nEnough about Sambora that's history and there's no admosity between them\n\n10\n\nView all 5 replies\n\nVeronique Marie\n\nDiana Kandiliotis\n\nHope he heads to Australia\n\n4","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2677.5394389987923,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}